          "description": "<p><strong>7:30PM</strong><br />\n<strong>Lobby doors open: 6:30PM</strong><br />\n<strong>Seating begins: 7PM</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tickets:</strong> $33, $45 + tax/fees<br />\n<strong>Student tickets:</strong> $10 + tax/fees</p>\n<p>We’re celebrating the season with music that is both reflective and radiant—sending audiences home with a melody in their hearts and a sense of holiday warmth. Our upcoming Holiday Pops concerts feature the full orchestra alongside VSO’s 80-voice chorus, leading spirited sing-alongs and performing festive favorites by Leroy Anderson, George Frideric Handel, Duke Ellington, and Georges Bizet. This year’s program also introduces two works new to VSO audiences: Margaret Bonds’ The Ballad of the Brown King, a powerful cantata honoring Balthazar with text by Langston Hughes, and Bob Krogstad’s Christmas at the Movies, a nostalgic medley featuring themes from The Grinch, The Polar Express, Miracle on 34th Street, and more. Beloved traditional carols round out this joyful, family-friendly holiday tradition.</p>",
